        "original_id": "f950b0f4-9c54-5b31-be86-8741723cf0bf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Montana, Glasgow\n- Roads: Montana Highway 42, Highway 24, U.S. Route 2\n- Rail Systems: BNSF Railway, Northern Transcon\n\nFacts:\n- The BNSF Railway operates the Northern Transcon, which follows the northernmost railroad route in the western United States.\n- Montana Highway 42 was formerly designated Highway 24W, and its number reverses the digits of 24.\n- Montana Highway 42 begins where Highway 24 crosses the BNSF Railway's Northern Transcon.\n- Montana Highway 42 runs northwest parallel to the Northern Transcon, then turns right in downtown Glasgow, passes under the railroad, and terminates at U.S. Route 2.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f36a5411-2159-598f-baf1-56da676e3c19",
        "text": "Page: Montana Highway 42. Sentence: Formerly Highway 24W, Highway 42 (its route number a reversal of \"24\") runs northwest from where Highway 24 crosses the BNSF Railway's Northern Transcon, staying parallel to the tracks until it turns right in Glasgow's downtown and dives under the railroad to meet with and terminate at U.S. Route 2.\nPage: Northern Transcon. Sentence: The Northern Transcon, a route operated by the BNSF Railway, traverses the most northerly route of any railroad in the western United States.",
